there are hundreds of small farming  villages in ukraine that were invaded  and occupied by the russians  this is the story of just one of them  on the road north out of kiev  alexander has hidden the clothes he was  wearing on the night the russians came  for him he's keeping them safe as  evidence of war crimes  he shows us the blood on his tracksuit  bottoms where a nail was hammered into  his knee  and the fabric that was used to tie his  hands behind his back  he has scars on his face where he was  burnt with cigarettes he doesn't want us  to identify him because he's scared that  the russians might return  there's no beer a soldier put my hands  on the table and hit them three times  with the butt of a machine gun my arm  was badly bent and broken alexander  tells us  he kept on saying you're a nazi you're a  nazi  they hit me so hard on my head i heard  something crack there was so much blood  on the floor that a soldier slipped in  it my nose was broken then they  threatened to cut my tendons and kill me  nearby is the house where they tortured  alexander and others in a room up on the  first floor he tells us  it is just a few doors down from the  village school  well what's left of it now  [Applause]  this became the main russian base when  they occupied the village  every single room has evidence of  rampant depravity  as a final insult they smeared their own  excrement on the walls and then fire  bomb the place as they retreated  [Music]  the russian soldiers went house to house  through the village marking front gates  if people lived inside  like everyone yulia vasilenko got a  knock on the door she's married to the  village policeman vyacheslav  he was taken away that day and he hasn't  been seen since  these are the stories of just one  ukrainian village  men women and children whose lives and  futures have been irrevocably changed  and damaged  during a hundred days of war  aleister bundle sky news in ukraine
 

